<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>4.14.0: Lesson Overview</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01113</md:content-id>
    <md:title>4.14.0: Lesson Overview</md:title>
    <md:uuid>499211f3-998c-4c54-968b-b72ccbe3bdad</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section id="sect-00001"><para id="para-00001">In this lesson, you will learn how to work with sequences and describe them recursively in an informal way. You will see how sequences are used to accomplish recurring tasks.</para>
<para id="para-00002">When you finish this lesson, you will be able to:</para>
<list id="list-00001">
  <item>Give examples of a sequence.</item>
  <item>Explain the meaning of the term “sequence.”</item>
  <item>Explain the meaning of the term “term,” as it is used in a mathematical sequence.</item>
</list>
<para id="para-00003">Here are the <emphasis>activities</emphasis> that will help you reach those goals:</para>
<list id="list-00002">
  <item>4.14.1: Describe the Pattern</item>
  <item>4.14.2: What Is a Sequence?  <list id="list-00003">
    <item>4.14.2: Self Check</item>
    <item>4.14.2: Additional Resources</item>
  </list></item>

  <item>4.14.3: The Connection Between Sequences and Terms <list id="list-00004">
    <item>4.14.3: Self Check</item>
    <item>4.14.3: Additional Resources</item>
  </list></item>
 
  <item>4.14.4: Rules for a Sequence</item>
</list>
<para id="para-00004">After that, you’ll <emphasis>practice and review</emphasis>.</para>
<list id="list-00005">
  <item>4.14.5: Practice</item>
  <item>4.14.6: Lesson Summary</item>
</list></section>
</content>
</document>
